<section class="service-section">
  <div class="section-container">
    <h2 class="section-title">Why Healthcare Workers Face Tax Problems</h2>
    <div class="service-content-full">
      <p>Healthcare workers—especially travel nurses, locum tenens physicians, and those with side practices—often have complex income situations. Multiple employers, 1099 consulting income, licensing fees across states, and housing stipends create a tax maze. What looks like a great income on paper can quickly become a tax nightmare.</p>
      <p>The good news? Currently Not Collectible (CNC) status tells the IRS that collecting from you right now would cause undue hardship. They pause all collection activity—no payments required—while you get your finances stabilized.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

